// Cosmetology license — the highest-volume beauty credential in the country.
//
// Read src/data/tracks/CONTRACT.md before editing. State variation IS the product here:
// required training hours run from 1,000 to 2,100 depending on the jurisdiction, a
// more-than-double spread, and the number moved in several states between 2022 and 2026 as
// part of occupational-licensing reform. California went 1,600 -> 1,000. Texas went
// 1,500 -> 1,000. Virginia went 1,500 -> 1,000. A 2024 hour table is already stale.
//
// The practical (hands-on) exam is the other moving part. California dropped it in 2022,
// Massachusetts in 2023, Mississippi in 2026, and Pennsylvania as far back as 2014.
// Minnesota never runs a hands-on exam at all — it uses a WRITTEN practical instead.
// A generic course will tell you to practise your mannequin work regardless. For a
// candidate in one of those states that is wasted money.
//
// 'unconfirmed' below means no primary source published it. It is never replaced with a
// number that looks about right. verified:true entries are honest compilations from the
// named secondary source and the app badges them as unverified.

